  "summary": [
    "Batch B, family B3 (`consecutive_in_path`). Five conjecture-local helpers (X3, X67, X91, X98, X114) now unfold to `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_consecutive p u v`: `u` and `v` are adjacent entries of the raw sequence `p`, in either order, i.e. `(u, v)` or `(v, u)` occurs in `zip p (behead p)` (equivalently `[:: u; v]` or `[:: v; u]` is an `infix` of `p`, `seq_consecutiveP`). Every helper had exactly that body with a Prop codomain, so all five are convertible to the canonical. No graph-edge, path, uniqueness or distinct-endpoint premise is added: the empty and one-entry sequences relate nothing and a repeated adjacent entry relates a value to itself (grounded in walks_paths.v and the public client).",
    "",
    "Six statements are affected: X3, X67, X91, X98 and X114 through their own files and X83 across modules (through `x83_rainbow_induced_path` and X3's `x3_induced_path`). Every chain is frozen in one certificate per area (helpers in `Legacy`, prefix-dropped chain copies and `statement` in per-row modules). X98 and X114 freeze their whole induced-subdivision record (type, constructor and seven fields, field prefixes dropped) and its `inhabited` wrapper; the frozen and live records are distinct inductive types, related by explicit mutually inverse field-by-field maps (`x98_induced_subdivision_model_compat`, `x114_induced_subdivision_model_compat`), through which the wrappers and statements are proved equivalent. X114 also freezes its decision problem `hisc_problem`; `x114_hisc_problem_compat` proves equivalent memberships and transfers the D7 layer's `in_NP` and `NP_hard`.",
    "",
    "Family B1 froze only the path-vertex chains of X3 and X67, so its snapshots `X3Legacy.statement` and `X67Legacy.theta` call the live `x3_induced_path` and `x67_induced_path_between`; they are kept verbatim and documented below as stale snapshots (B1's and B2's certificates over them still hold, as conversions). `X3Original` and `X67Original` freeze those statements end to end, over B1's frozen path-vertex objects (listed below as `b1-frozen`, with B1's certificates) and this family's chains, with `*_original_compat` certificates to the live statements.",
    "",
    "Kernel evidence, independent of this textual report: `Print All Dependencies` of the six frozen statements and the two originals contains no live helper or chain declaration of this family and not `seq_consecutive`, the frozen record types are checked by conversion (`Print All Dependencies` lists constants only), and each live statement reaches `seq_consecutive` and its alias (/srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/B3-consecutive_in_path/print_all_dependencies_summary.txt, with the probes and the full output beside it).",
    "",
    "No statement text, doc block, manifest row or leg state changes (checked below), so the documented discrepancies of the affected rows stay verbatim, including X114's relational complexity proxy, X98's coefficient-list polynomial, X3's exactly-s-vertex path and X67's solved status. The cyclic variants `consecutive_in_cycle` (X3, X91 and four others, over `zip c (rot 1 c)`) were classified here as the next family and were later migrated by B4 (family consecutive-in-cycle, report `consecutive_in_cycle`), so they are no longer listed as untouched variants."
  ],
